Chapter: GopFat16GeomGuardTest
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopXhci
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Foreword chapter Gpt
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The negative control for gfat-geometry-ok. The .disk sidecar is the valid
 gop-fat16 image with ONE change: the BPB reserved-sector count (offset 14) is
 0xFFFF, so fat-start lands far past the end of the medium. That is volume
 geometry, not a read length, so the mount must REFUSE rather than serve the
 wrong sectors. esp-start=64 proves GPT parsing still succeeds and bps is still
 512, so a refusal here is the geometry guard and nothing earlier; stage 8 is
 gfat-stage-geom. Ablate gfat-geometry-ok and this flips to geom-mount-ok=1
 stage=7 -- the mount accepts a volume that reads off the medium.

Section: Main

  show-esp : [Device.Port] Text
  show-esp = act
    s <- gpt-esp-start
    "esp-start=" & show s
  end

  show-guard : [Device.Port] Text
  show-guard = act
    m <- gfat-mount-esp
    "geom-mount-ok=" & show (if m.gm-ok then 1 else 0)
      & " stage=" & show (xdiag-get gfat-cell-stage)
  end

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    a <- show-esp
    print-line-uni a
    b <- show-guard
    print-line-uni b
  end
